Actual rendered line: `- tool_use toolu_x sha256:… — {"paths":"src/a.ts,C:\\q\\outside\\x.txt"}`. Control: the single-path value {"file_path":"C:\\q\\outside\\x.txt"} is correctly WITHHELD (absLike→inside=false), and a multi-path value whose extra piece is a host-denied in-project path ({"file":"src/a.ts,private/deny.txt"}, {"file":"src/a.ts,.env"}) is correctly WITHHELD by the name screen — proving the gap is specifically the out-of-project embedded path. Realistic because tool pointers are captured for all tool calls, and for any non-built-in/MCP tool the preview is the canonical JSON (store.argsPreview), previewString keeps single interior spaces, and a 'paths' field is a path list for many tools.
